              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "organizar — \"to organise\". A regular -ar verb, so its one-word future follows falar: Organizarei tudo. — \"I will organise everything.\" In everyday speech: Vou organizar tudo."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "organizar from French organiser (EtymDB 2.1) — borrowed. Behind it is Medieval Latin organizare, from Latin organum, \"tool, instrument\"."
            }
